          "update_time": 1793129900.986,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "I would test a **theta-modular weight applied directly to the physical Wronskian**. My previous reply was too definite: I had identified an open direction, but had not selected this particular construction.\n\nWrite \\(\\vartheta_j(x)=\\theta_j(0\\mid i e^{2x})\\), and choose the explicit weight\n\\[\n\\mu(x)=\\frac{\\vartheta_2(x)^4}{\\vartheta_3(x)^4},\n\\qquad\nw(x)=4\\mu(x)\\bigl(1-\\mu(x)\\bigr).\n\\]\nTheta identities give \\(w(0)=1\\), positivity, and the reflection symmetry \\(w(-x)=w(x)\\). Thus the weight is determined by the canonical theta source, independently of any physical zeros. [DLMF theta identities](https://dlmf.nist.gov/20.7)\n\nFor our unchanged forced equation, set\n\\[\nY_{xx}+\\lambda Y=g_t,\\qquad Z=\\partial_\\lambda Y,\n\\qquad W=YZ_x-Y_xZ.\n\\]\nThe proposed current is simply \\(\\mathcal J=wW\\). Its complete identity is\n\\[\nY(0)B_\\lambda-BZ(0)\n=\\int_0^\\infty\n\\underbrace{\\left[wY^2+w g_tZ-w'W\\right]}_{\\text{all three terms retained}}\\,dx,\n\\qquad B=Y_x(0).\n\\]\nAt a candidate collision, \\(B=B_\\lambda=0\\), so this integral must vanish.\n\n**The actual test is whether the shared theta structure of \\(w\\) and \\(g_t\\) constrains that cancellation.** Their derivatives can be expressed through the finite nonlinear system for the theta constants and \\(E_2\\). That supplies a specific algebraic framework for examining the full integrand. [Theta differential system, Proposition 1](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1012.1429)\n\nI would make the first investigation narrow:\n\n- Substitute the exact theta equations and determine whether they produce a useful signed remainder or comparison on a stated time–frequency domain.\n- Check the proposed estimate against the known collision controls, identifying exactly which canonical relation each control lacks.\n- Stop if the calculation only reproduces the boundary identity or requires dropping the \\(w'W\\) term.\n\nThis falls outside the earlier finite **linear** circle-closure obstruction. **It remains an untested multiplier proposal:** the weighted identity alone supplies no collision exclusion, and I do not yet have evidence that its signed estimate will succeed."
            ]
